Overall: \
	This is an attempt to implement Raft system using Akka Finite State Machine. The implemented aspects inlude voting mechanism and log replication, not includes the execution in state machines or state machine replication.  The program is written according to figure 2 in the Raft paper with most of the variable names adopting the names used in the figure as well. \
\
\
	The program have implemented \'93NodeData\'94 class which stores data that are supposed to be stored on a server. The FSM actor implements the operation when it receives certain message in a certain state. \
	\
	There is another non-FSM actor class \'93Client\'94, these actors act as client and sends \'93Raw messages \'94  to all the actors, while only FSM actors in the state \'93Leader \'94 has function \'93leaderReceiveClientMessage\'94 implemented to handle it. \
\
 \
\
Run: \
\
     	Use IntelliJ to run the program, the main function is in DiningHakkersOnFsm.java\
	The .java files are all in ./src/main/java/sample.fsm\
\
\
Results:\
\
	The program have all the messages sending and receiving enabled. \
	The nodes has been observed in all three states. \
	\
\
Resources:   Akka java documentations.  \
		some documentation about java function such as manipulation about array list etc. \
