Bugs:\
	1. After running the program for some time the term of the node are usually much larger than the term of the message(therefore the term of the sending actor), this might be because in some places the term on the node is not updated by the message term properly. \
\
\
	2. Since HeartBeatRPC is supposed to be a special case of AppendEntry RPC, according to the Raft paper, a server(any follower or leader) receiving this message should restart the timeout if their terms are the same. But if I do restart the timer, which I already commented out in the function \'93followerReceiveHeartBeatRPC\'94 line 6&7, the program will get stuck in term 1.  \
\
\
	3. Although the program is observed to execute function \'93handleAppendEntryRPC\'94, but I haven\'92t do Logging for how the server logs changes, therefore it\'92s not very obvious whether they have been replicated successfully. But all the functionality has been implemented including initializing and updating the nextIndex and matchIndex HashMap and updating the commitIndex. \
\
\
	4. Maybe better logging can be done to better check the program. \
